course: dictionary
lesson: 6333
title: Moult: losing and growing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To moult means to lose feathers, fur, hair or skin so that new ones can grow. Birds moult feathers, dogs moult hair, and snakes shed skin.
explain: Context gives clues. «An insect's hard outer skeleton cannot stretch, so a growing insect must moult.» The words cannot stretch and must show that the old covering has to come off before the insect can grow bigger.
explain: Moult can also be a noun. In «many crabs can grow back a lost claw over several moults», moults means the times it happens. In American English the spelling is molt.
fact: To moult means to lose feathers, fur, hair or skin so that new ones can grow.
fact: Moult can be a verb (they moult) or a noun (a moult).
fact: In American English the word is spelled «molt».
fact: «Arctic foxes moult from white in winter to brown or grey in summer so they match snow and then rocks.»
fact: «A caterpillar moults about 4 or 5 times as it grows.»
exercise: «An insect's hard outer skeleton cannot stretch, so a growing insect must moult.» Why must a growing insect moult? | It is ill and needs to rest | It wants to change its colour for the winter | *Its hard outer skin cannot stretch, so it must come out of the old one
exercise: What does moult mean? | To run fast across the snow | To hide under rocks until spring | To eat a lot of food before winter | *To lose feathers, fur, hair or skin so that new ones can grow
exercise: In «many crabs can grow back a lost claw over several moults», what kind of word is moults? | A noun, meaning a claw | An adjective, meaning very big | *A noun, meaning the times a crab loses its shell | A verb, meaning to run away
test: What do dogs moult? | Eggs | Bones | *Hair | Feathers
test: The American spelling of moult is which? | mole | malt | mould | *molt
exam: Which sentence uses moult as a verb? | The fox has a thick winter moult | The caterpillar had its fourth moult | A moult is a sign of growing | *The bird will moult its feathers in the autumn
